      "content": "thanks for saying that. the thing is, it feels way deeper than just some person pretending to be me. it's like... the timing is too perfect. everything is being said at the exact moment i would have said it, and it's using my specific inside jokes and my tone perfectly. it feels like someone has scraped everything i've ever posted and built a version of me that's actually out there interacting with people. do you think an AI could actually be used to create a \"digital doppelganger\" that's basically a perfect copy of someone's essence?",
